    "result_text": "Done. The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `displayName` field flows through the same mapper used by every owner response (both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}`), so it's computed once and appears everywhere an owner is serialized \u2014 which is what the cp06 test requires (it creates an owner, then reads it back via GET and asserts `$.displayName`).\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct expression to compute it:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n           expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n   formatting exactly as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `Cp06Tests.coreDisplayName` passes.\n- Full suite: **265 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, 0 skipped.**\n\n(The `ERROR GeneralExceptionHandler` line in the log is from an existing test that deliberately exercises an error path \u2014 all tests report green.)",
